         "id": "SECTION_images",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Images from San Jose CR Museo\n\nThese images are copyright for San Jose CR Museo and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgSanJoseCR0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgSanJoseCR0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Metate to grind corn from the Postclassic period. Photo taken on <htdate0>, during a visit to the Anthropological Museum in San José, Costa Rica (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Are we truly equal? - In this text, we explore the acceptable limits of inequality and emphasize that within our species, there are no races. (<htcite1>)</li><li>Understanding the Multiplication Table (4 and 5) - In this text, we examine the relationship between triangles and mountains. (<htcite2>)</li><li>Classifying equality - In this text, we see that classifying is more than comparing things that are exactly alike. (<htcite3>)</li><li>Playing with Consonants and Vowels - An interactive game to understand how syllables are created. (<htcite4>)</li><li>Multiplying the Findings - an educational game in which the reader visualizes multiplication while exploring different archaeological sites. (<htcite5>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part I) - In this first stage, learning is reinforced by completing number sequences that go up to the hundreds, helping to consolidate the understanding of basic foundations. (<htcite6>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part II) - Continuing the challenge, this stage presents sequences that extend up to the billions, deepening the mastery of numerical patterns. (<htcite7>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgSanJoseCR1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgSanJoseCR1', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Musical instruments. Photo taken on <htdate1>, during a visit to the Anthropological Museum in San José, Costa Rica (<htcite8>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Returning - In this text, we present the subtraction operation as a form of return. (<htcite9>)</li><li>Counting - We introduce the idea of counting using our body. (<htcite10>)</li><li>Playing with Consonants and Vowels - An interactive game to understand how syllables are created. (<htcite11>)</li><li>Multiplying the Findings - an educational game in which the reader visualizes multiplication while exploring different archaeological sites. (<htcite12>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part I) - In this first stage, learning is reinforced by completing number sequences that go up to the hundreds, helping to consolidate the understanding of basic foundations. (<htcite13>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part II) - Continuing the challenge, this stage presents sequences that extend up to the billions, deepening the mastery of numerical patterns. (<htcite14>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
